AUDIO: 'Hi everyone. In this guide, we\'ll walk you through how to get the best possible results with Splatica. This video provides step-by-step instructions for 360° video capture. This is what we\'re aiming for: sharp, clean geometry, full coverage,'

[00:13] [scene:concept]
VISUAL: Comparison of "GOOD" and "BAD" 3D reconstructions, showing warped surfaces, missing sections, and motion blur in the bad example.
AUDIO: 'consistent lighting, and no visible artifacts. If you don\'t follow this guide, you may end up with bad results like warped surfaces, missing sections, or motion blur. Step one, choose the right time.'

[00:25] [scene:instructions]
VISUAL: Step 1: Choose Your Shooting Time & Location, with examples for outdoor and indoor lighting.
AUDIO: 'Outdoors, shoot in good weather during the day. The more natural light, the better. Indoors, choose daytime if there are windows, and turn on all available lighting. Next, prepare your scene. Ensure nothing is moving, remove'

[00:39] [scene:instructions]
VISUAL: Step 2: Equipment Setup, detailing camera and selfie stick preparation.
AUDIO: 'unnecessary objects, and lock everything in place. Open curtains and blinds to let in as much light as possible. Double-check everything before you hit record. Step two, equipment setup. Attach the camera to a selfie stick,'

[00:53] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'which helps capture more space without obstructing the operator. Check your camera, clean lenses, full battery, enough storage, and updated firmware. Step three, basic camera settings. Swipe down to see the settings. Set your'

[01:07] [scene:instructions]
VISUAL: Step 3: Basic camera settings for Insta360, showing UI for H.265, high bitrate, and high sharpness. Step 5: Shooting settings, showing Insta360 UI for manual mode (M) and recommended shutter speed, ISO, and white balance for different lighting conditions.
AUDIO: 'camera for the best quality. Use H.265, high bit rate, and high video sharpness. Step four, shooting mode. Push shooting mode, choose video, and select the 360° mode. Step five, shooting settings.'

[01:21] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Swipe from the right and push M for manual mode. Adjust your shutter speed, ISO, and white balance based on the light conditions, as listed on the screen.'

[01:33] [scene:instructions]
VISUAL: Step 6: Shooting specification settings, showing Insta360 UI for resolution (8K, 5.7K) and frame rate (60, 30).
AUDIO: 'Step six, shooting specification settings. Swipe up from the bottom. Set the resolution and frame rate depending on lighting. In low light, move slower to avoid motion blur. Step seven, movement rules. Move slowly and smoothly at about'

[01:46] [scene:instructions]
VISUAL: Step 7: Movement rules, illustrating slow, even movement in an arc and maintaining distance from objects. Step 8: Full Coverage — 3 heights, 4 Passes, detailing main, lower, upper, and main back passes.
AUDIO: '1 to 1.5 m/s. Do not rotate in one spot. Keep some distance from walls and objects, and avoid sudden movements. Step eight, full coverage. Capture the scene in four passes at three different'

[01:59] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'heights. Pass one is the main pass at chest level. Pass two is lower, at hip level. Pass three is upper, overhead. Pass four is the main pass, but in the opposite direction. Do not stop'

[02:11] [scene:instructions]
VISUAL: Trajectories for outdoor (zigzag, spiral) and indoor shooting, with optimal recording times.
AUDIO: 'recording between passes. Plan your movement path. Outdoors, use zigzags for facades or spirals for objects. Indoors, walk the perimeter and add a diagonal pass. Aim for two to four minutes of'

[02:23] [scene:instructions]
VISUAL: Quality Control checklist for reviewing footage.
AUDIO: 'footage. Up to six minutes is acceptable. Finally, quality control. Review your video. Check for motion blur, flickering, brightness jumps, and missed sections. If anything looks off, reshoot right away.'

[02:37] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'To upload your footage to Splatica, first connect your camera via USB and copy the source.insv file. Open app.splatica.com and upload the .insv file directly. Do not convert it to MP4, use third-party'

[02:50] [scene:summary]
VISUAL: Final Control Sheet summarizing camera, scene, and shooting checks.
AUDIO: 'editors, or rename the file, as this can affect scene orientation or break the results. Before finishing, use this final control sheet to check your work. Ensure the camera is ready, the scene is'

